  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 1237 PM CDT Mon Jun 15 2026\n\nThe hottest conditions so far this summer are expected for\nWednesday and Thursday as high pressure aloft moves across the\narea. Weak surface low will develop over West Texas, with a\ndryline shifting east towards West Central Texas each afternoon.\nFor areas west of the dryline, downslope west winds will push\ntemperatures well in excess of 100 degrees, perhaps into the 105+\nrange. For areas east of the dryline, temperatures near 100 will\ncombine with high humidity values to push heat index values into\nthe 105+. Thursday may be the hottest day as the surface low\ninches closer to the area and a front approaches from the north,\nallowing for some prefrontal compressional heating as well. \nEither way, chance of a heat advisory for either temperature or \nheat index is medium to high (60-80+) by Thursday, and only a \nlittle lower for Wednesday.\n\nNext cold front will push across the area Thursday night into \nFriday and bring a chance of showers and storms back into the\nforecast. Much like the ongoing forecast, this chance of storms\nwill pass and the heat will return with temperatures pushing to\nnear 100 in some areas.",
